💡 **SUGGESTION: whitespace-only `baseUrl` short-circuits the fallback chain**

The `||` chain picks the first *truthy* candidate, but a whitespace-only string is truthy yet trims to `''` — so `resolveJiraBaseUrl({ tracker: { baseUrl: ' ' }, jira: { baseUrl: 'https://jira.example.com' } })` returns `''` and silently drops links even though a valid `jira.baseUrl` (or `JIRA_BASE_PATH` env) is set. Same for a whitespace-only `jira.baseUrl` masking the env fallback.

Trim each candidate before the chain so blank-after-trim values fall through:

```javascript
function resolveJiraBaseUrl(config) {
    var trackerBase = String(_sectionOf(config, 'tracker').baseUrl || '').trim();
    var jiraBase = String(_sectionOf(config, 'jira').baseUrl || '').trim();
    var raw = trackerBase || jiraBase || _readJiraBasePathEnv();
    return String(raw || '').trim().replace(/\/+$/, '');
}
